1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:04,320
足迹图课程，第9单元，拍卖不平衡
The Footprint course, unit 9, auction imbalances.

2
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:06,660
这是30天挑战的第15天
This is challenge day 15 of 30.

3
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:13,880
接下来的幻灯片，我们将聚焦成功交易员的高效交易习惯
In the following slide, we are going to focus on the highly effective trading habits of successful traders.

5
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:21,480
现在，重点是培养和发展你自己的习惯，为你带来微小优势
Now, the focus is on creating and developing your own habits that can give you marginal edges.

7
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:27,082
你将看到Axia交易员的一些高效习惯示例
You’re going to see a couple of examples of some of the effective habits traders at Axia have,

8
00:00:27,082 --> 00:00:30,975
但最终，你要采纳并发展这些习惯——属于你自己的
but ultimately, you want to adopt some of these and develop them—your own.

10
00:00:56,540 --> 00:01:01,040
第一个：强迫性早间例行程序
The first one: obsessive morning routine.

11
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:09,740
最成功的交易员，不只是Axia的，整个伦敦金融城的，都有这种强迫性早间例行程序
The most successful traders, not just at Axia, but across the city of London, they have this obsessive morning routine.

14
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:15,720
所谓‘强迫性’，是说他们每周一到周五都在同一时间到岗
By ‘obsessive,’ I mean they are there at the exact same time, Monday to Friday.

16
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,780
这是强迫性的，是纪律的体现
It’s obsessive. It’s disciplined.

17
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,138
我们说的是一些最大的交易员，不只是伦敦的，而是全球的
We’re talking about some of the biggest traders, not just in the city, but in the world,

18
00:01:23,138 --> 00:01:27,135
他们做这份工作10年、15年，仍然每天早上6:30到岗
who have been doing this job for 10, 15 years, still coming in at 6:30 a.m.

21
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:33,540
现在，这背后有原因，这已成为他们成功的关键
Now, there’s a reason for that. It has become so imperative to their success,

23
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:40,080
他们几乎在6:30之后的任何时间到岗，都难以成功
they could almost not be successful by arriving at any point after 6:30 a.m.

25
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:45,440
所以，这是一个真正的习惯，是一个习惯，早上6:30到岗是习惯
So, that is a real habit. It’s a habit. Being in at 6:30 a.m. is a habit.

27
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:50,580
下一个：交易机会，而不是交易时间
The next one: trade the opportunity, not the clock.

28
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:52,820
成功的交易员——没有时间限制
Successful traders—there is no clock.

29
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:55,410
我的伴侣经常对我的作息很沮丧
My partner gets very frustrated with me a lot of the time

30
00:01:55,410 --> 00:01:57,720
因为他总问，你几点回家
because he always says, What time are you going to get home?

32
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:58,560
你什么时候回来
When are you going to be back?

33
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:01,220
我说，‘谁知道呢？’
And I say, 'Well, who knows? Okay?'

34
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:05,360
交易时没有时间概念，只有机会
There is no clock when it comes to trading. There are only opportunities.

35
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:10,874
如果市场在波动，如果日本央行有动作，如果澳大利亚有事件
If the markets are moving around, if there’s a Bank of Japan, if there’s something going on in Australia,

36
00:02:10,874 --> 00:02:13,596
而我们在交易欧洲市场，就没有时间限制
and we’re trading the European markets, there is no clock.

39
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:15,040
我们不在乎钟表显示几点
We don’t care what the clock says.

40
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:17,160
我们只为机会而来
We’re there for the opportunity.

41
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:20,380
在职业生涯早期就养成这个习惯
Form the habit early in your career.

42
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:24,720
当市场出现机会时，别看时间
When the markets exhibit opportunity, don’t look at the clock, okay?

44
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:25,780
别按时间工作
Don’t work to a clock.

45
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,200
按机会工作
Work to the opportunity.

46
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:31,488
这是我职业生涯早期就注意到的事
That is something that, again, very early in my career, I noticed

47
00:02:31,488 --> 00:02:34,179
不仅是日内交易员，现在依然如此
about day traders, but also even at this point.

49
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:36,880
最成功的交易员不会看时间
The most successful traders don’t look at the clock.

50
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:38,020
他们只盯着机会
They look at the opportunities.

51
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:42,440
健康饮食，健康生活方式，健康心态
Healthy diet, healthy lifestyle, healthy mind, okay?

52
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:44,880
这不是秘密，你来我们交易大厅
It’s no secret. You come onto our trading floor,

53
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:46,800
看看交易员早餐吃什么
and you look at what the guy’s eating for breakfast.

54
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:48,780
看看他们午餐吃什么
You look at what they’re eating for lunch, okay?

55
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:52,360
我保证他们不会吃高糖食物，不会吃加工食品
I can guarantee you it’s not high-sugar diets, all right? It’s not processed diets.

56
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:56,560
大部分时候，我是说，就连我身后这位，他吃的东西让人难以置信
Most of the time, I mean, even the guy behind me—it’s incredible the things he eats.

58
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:58,977
我们说的是早餐吃三文鱼和菠菜
We’re talking salmon and spinach for breakfast,

59
00:02:58,977 --> 00:03:02,603
然后是各种各样营养丰富的健康食物
and then we’re talking all sorts of crazy, nutritious, healthy food

60
00:03:04,117 --> 00:03:04,419
为什么？
Why?

61
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:08,073
因为说到底，如果你要坐在那里
Because at the end of the day, if you've got to sit there

62
00:03:08,073 --> 00:03:10,533
连续10、12小时保持专注，发挥巅峰状态
for 10, 12 hours and focus and perform at the peak,

63
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:13,540
健康的生活方式是关键
A healthy lifestyle.

65
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:15,520
交易员不会在工作日出去喝酒
Traders don’t go out drinking during the week, okay?

66
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:20,104
推特上那些坐在海滩上，喝着啤酒
These Twitter pictures of people sitting on a beach, drinking a beer,

67
00:03:20,104 --> 00:03:23,317
用笔记本电脑交易的照片——那都是胡扯
trading off a laptop—that is absolute bullshit, guys.

69
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:25,920
我真心希望你们知道那纯属胡说八道
I really, really hope you know it’s absolute rubbish.

70
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:31,236
健康的生活方式就是坐在交易桌前，保持健康
A healthy lifestyle is being at the desk, healthy,

71
00:03:31,236 --> 00:03:35,592
确保自己获得充足睡眠
making sure you get the maximum amount of sleep,

72
00:03:35,592 --> 00:03:40,432
思想上始终专注，思想上始终强大
that you’re mentally always focused, mentally always strong, okay?

73
00:03:40,432 --> 00:03:41,400
规律锻炼
Regular exercise.

75
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,545
在任何一天，我们大多数交易员都会进行某种锻炼
On any given day, most of our traders will be doing some form of exercise,

76
00:03:46,545 --> 00:03:48,969
无论是骑自行车上下班
whether that’s cycling to and from work,

77
00:03:48,969 --> 00:03:53,819
还是周三在Axia团队一起做瑜伽
whether that’s doing yoga on Wednesdays, which we do regularly at AXIA as a team,

78
00:03:53,819 --> 00:03:55,637
无论是训练半程铁人三项
whether that’s doing half-Ironman training,

79
00:03:55,637 --> 00:03:58,668
还是练巴西柔术，还是练踢拳道
whether that’s doing jiu-jitsu, whether that’s doing kickboxing,

80
00:04:02,313 --> 00:04:04,738
而且很多时候，猜猜怎么着？
And a lot of the time, guess what?

84
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:07,440
他们是一起锻炼的。为什么？因为他们在互相激励
They’re doing it together. Why? Because they’re pushing each other,

85
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:11,820
因为他们知道，规律锻炼是必须养成的习惯，否则交易表现会下滑
because they know that regular exercise is a habit they have to have, otherwise their performance sinks.

87
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:16,260
然后是整点交易
Then, top-of-the-hour trading.

88
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:18,800
这同样是我职业生涯早期学到的
Again, something I learned very early in my career:

89
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:26,540
日内交易员的成功程度会告诉你——他们总坐在交易桌前
The degree of success as a day trader will tell you—they’re always at their desk.

91
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:29,257
尽可能在整点时刻交易，明白吗
At the top of the hour as best as possible, Okay?

92
00:04:29,257 --> 00:04:31,480
因为很多时候
And it’s because a lot of the time,

93
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:35,679
新闻发布和央行官员的评论总会在整点出现
news releases and commentary from central bankers always tends to come at the top of the hour.

95
00:04:46,290 --> 00:04:53,457
如果他们要出去吃午饭，不会在12点前1分钟，而是12点过1分钟
If they wanted to go out for lunch, it wasn’t at one minute to 12, it was one minute past 12.

98
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:59,020
他们培养了这个习惯。为什么？因为长期来看，这个习惯能为他们赚钱
They developed this habit. Why? Because in the long run, this habit made them money.

100
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,639
赢单和亏单的交易例行程序——
Winning trade routines and losing trade routines—

101
00:05:01,639 --> 00:05:05,629
这是一个很棒的习惯——坐在我对面的一个交易员
A fantastic habit—one of the guys who sits opposite me,

102
00:05:05,629 --> 00:05:09,619
每次亏损时，我都能听到他的沮丧
every time he takes a loss, I can hear the frustration,

103
00:05:11,433 --> 00:05:13,972
我知道他的持仓状况
I know the position he’s in.

104
00:05:13,972 --> 00:05:20,138
但每次亏损后，他会站起来，推好椅子，然后离开
But every time he takes that loser, he gets up, pushes his chair in, and walks away.

106
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:24,120
离开3、4分钟，再回来，重新开始
Takes three or four minutes away, comes back, starts again.

108
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:32,340
这是他为自己量身定制的绝佳交易例行程序，而且很有效。同样，赢单的交易例行程序——
It’s a fantastic trade routine he’s developed for himself that works for him. Equally, a winning trade routine—

109
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:38,980
一些最成功的交易员，在完美执行交易后，会奖励自己
Some of the most successful traders, when they execute to perfection, they reward themselves.

112
00:05:39,200 --> 00:05:45,473
他们会站起来，离开座位，给自己一个心理确认：‘你干得很出色’
They stand up, they walk away, give themselves that mental checkmark: 'You’ve done the job well.'

115
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:49,580
然后重置，再次开始
then reset, and start again.

116
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:58,660
风险热身。同样，我打赌你们大多数人从未想过‘风险热身’这个概念
Risk warm-up. Again, I bet most of you have never thought about the concept of risk warm-up.

118
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:00,620
作为交易员，我们必须热身，就像职业运动员一样
As traders, we have to warm up, just like professional athletes.

119
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:06,660
为什么？因为早上一开始，你对风险的理解和一天后完全不同
Why? Because first thing in the morning, your conceptualization of risk is very different from later in the day.

120
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:11,140
为什么？因为随着一天的推进
Why? Because over the period of the day,

121
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:13,607
你会接很多单，对吧
You're taking on a lot of trades, right?

122
00:06:13,607 --> 00:06:17,679
这意味着你已经对‘风险’的概念热身了
Which means that you are warmed up to the concept of what risk means.

124
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:23,200
而且，你在早上对风险的规避程度和一天后差别很大
And you're far more or far less risk-averse first thing in the morning than you are later in the day.

127
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:29,520
明白吗？你需要时间进入状态，进入节奏，理解风险所在
Okay? It takes you time to get into the flow, into the momentum, into understanding where the risk is.

130
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:35,400
所以，大多数职业交易员都有个习惯：早上一开始，他们会减小仓位规模
So, most professional traders have a habit, first thing in the morning, they reduce their clip size.

133
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:40,960
他们在一天早些时候承担更少风险，直到热身完毕，然后再增加风险
They risk less early in the day, until they're warmed up, and then they increase their risk.

135
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:45,360
结构化的早间简报和午后复盘
Structured, exact morning briefing and afternoon debrief.

136
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:50,740
你任何早上来我们办公室，问交易员‘能看看你的早间表格吗？’
You come into our office any morning, and you ask a trader, 'Can I see your morning sheet?'

139
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:55,089
猜猜怎么着？他们填的都是一样的早间交易表格
And guess what? They’re filling in the exact same morning trade sheet

140
00:06:55,089 --> 00:06:58,219
可能已经坚持了好几年
that they’ve done, probably for a couple of years.

142
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:02,480
他们为什么这么做，其实没有秘密
And again, there’s no secret as to why they do it.

144
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:08,600
但这种结构化的早间简报，让他们在市场开盘前进入特定心态
But that structured morning briefing allows them to be in a very specific mindset before the markets open.

147
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:10,300
这是一种叫做预热心态的技巧
Okay? It’s a technique called priming.

148
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:15,940
你必须在开盘前调整心态
You’ve got to prime your mind to be in the right mental state before the market opens.

150
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:18,880
所以，每天早上你都要预热大脑
Okay? So, every morning, you prime your brain.

151
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:21,640
为市场开盘做好准备
To be ready come the open of the markets.

152
00:07:22,220 --> 00:07:23,720
午后也是一样
It's the same thing in the afternoon.

153
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:27,680
我们最成功的交易员，他的做法特别棒
Our most successful trader, Okay? And it's so wonderful.

155
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:32,240
这是我特别弱的地方，但我有幸见证了很久
It's something that I'm very weak at, and I've been so fortunate to see for so long now.

158
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:34,520
他的午后复盘特别出色
His afternoon debriefs are incredible.

159
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:38,700
他用印象笔记记录，已经坚持快6年了
I mean, he's got this set of Evernotes that dates back for almost six years.

161
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:44,400
你要看到他完成记录的简洁方式，会感到不可思议
And if you see the concise manner in which it's completed, it is incredible.

163
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:49,200
你会坐在那里赞叹‘哇，难怪这家伙成功’
You will sit there in awe, going, 'Wow, I can see why this guy is successful.'

165
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:54,960
因为他在每天交易结束时，特别注重细节
Because he pays so much attention to detail when completing his trading at the end of the day.

168
00:07:56,260 --> 00:07:57,000
第九点
Number nine.

169
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:04,200
对基本面敏感的市场，这和交易机会而非交易时间有关
Fundamentally sensitive markets. Now, this ties in a little bit with trading the opportunity, not the clock.

171
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:09,569
我们两位非常成功的交易员，当市场对基本面更敏感时
Two of our very successful traders, when the markets have become more fundamentally sensitive,

172
00:08:09,569 --> 00:08:13,811
也就是说，市场对小道消息更敏感
in other words, they're a little bit more sensitive to little comments.

173
00:08:13,811 --> 00:08:16,639
不一定是基本面重大新闻，而是些小道消息
Not necessarily fundamentally moving news, but little comments.

176
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:20,640
他们会尽可能长时间守在那里
They will sit there for as long as humanly possible.

177
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:26,298
即使意味着熬到晚上11点，早上6点又来
If that means staying there until 11 o'clock at night, and then coming in at six o'clock in the morning,

179
00:08:28,894 --> 00:08:29,759
他们不动
They don't move.

181
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,040
不出去吃饭
They don't go out to eat.

182
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:32,220
不上厕所
They don't go to the bathroom.

183
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:36,440
就坐在那里交易这些对基本面敏感的市场
They just sit there and trade the fundamentally sensitive markets.

184
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:42,189
最后一点：我见过的每一位成功交易员
Then, the last one: Every single successful trader I've ever seen,

185
00:08:42,189 --> 00:08:46,138
我有幸见过很多这样的交易员
and I've been so lucky to see a lot of them,

186
00:08:46,138 --> 00:08:47,935
他们执行得非常简单
they keep the execution simple.

189
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:50,280
他们不会尝试金字塔加仓
They don't try and pyramid.

190
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:51,720
他们不会尝试摊平成本
They're not looking to average.

191
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:56,580
也不会去追求各种疯狂、奇特的想法
They're not looking to do all sorts of crazy and wonderful, exotic kinds of ideas.

193
00:08:57,100 --> 00:09:01,620
他们只用最简单的交易策略
They do the most simplistic trade strategies.

194
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:06,901
这正是让我合作过的每一个人成功的原因
And that is what makes, not just every single person I've worked with,

195
00:09:06,901 --> 00:09:09,856
甚至可能是全球每个交易员成功的原因
but probably every single trader across the world.

198
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:13,882
对吧？这就是10个高效习惯
Right? These are 10 highly effective habits,

199
00:09:13,882 --> 00:09:21,238
如果你能在交易中落实它们
that, if you can implement them into your trading, you will start to see results.

200
00:09:21,238 --> 00:09:22,218
你肯定会看到效果，1000%保证
1,000% guaranteed. Okay?

201
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:23,700
因为这些习惯经过了验证和测试
Because they have been tried and tested.

202
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:26,460
被我见过的每个交易员都在使用
They've been utilized across every single trader I've ever seen.

203
00:09:26,460 --> 00:09:33,140
但这并不意味着，拥有这10个习惯你就会立刻赚钱
Now, it's not to say that if you have all 10 of these, you will suddenly start making money. Okay?

205
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:34,800
现在揭开真相
Let's pull the wool from your eyes.

206
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:37,740
事实并非如此。但它想告诉你的是：
